{"black_box_warning":{"current_value":"No FDA boxed warning identified in selected current DailyMed label.","fda_source_urls":["https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%22f280bbd8-2af2-444a-bd96-e409337ca6dd%22&limit=5","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2023/209501s005lbl.pdf"],"proposed_value":"No FDA boxed warning identified in selected current FDA/openFDA label.","rationale":"The no-boxed-warning conclusion is supportable only with FDA/openFDA or FDA label sources. The current wording and source rely on DailyMed, which is not permissible for this field.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect"},"blocking_questions":[],"fact_checks":[{"current_value":"pregabalin","field":"generic_name","proposed_value":"pregabalin","rationale":"FDA/Drugs@FDA labeling and EMA/eMC records identify the active substance as pregabalin.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2016/021446s030%2C022488s010lbl.pdf","https://www.ema.europa.eu/en/medicines/human/EPAR/lyrica","https://www.medicines.org.uk/emc/product/1757/smpc"]},{"current_value":"Yes","field":"available_in_us","proposed_value":"Yes","rationale":"FDA labeling and Drugs@FDA records support U.S. approval/availability for Lyrica/pregabalin products.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2016/021446s030%2C022488s010lbl.pdf","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/nda/2004/021446_Lyrica%20Capsules_approv.PDF"]},{"current_value":"2005","field":"year_fda_cleared","proposed_value":"2004","rationale":"FDA labeling states Initial U.S. Approval: 2004, and the original approval letter is dated December 30, 2004. The row value 2005 is not supported as the initial FDA approval year.","requires_user_approval":true,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2016/021446s030%2C022488s010lbl.pdf","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/nda/2004/021446_Lyrica%20Capsules_approv.PDF"]},{"current_value":"Focal","field":"epilepsy_type","proposed_value":"Focal","rationale":"FDA and eMC labeling support adjunctive therapy for partial-onset/partial seizures, corresponding to focal seizures. The Lyrica CR label alone should not be used for this fact because CR failed to demonstrate efficacy as adjunctive therapy for partial-onset seizures.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2016/021446s030%2C022488s010lbl.pdf","https://www.medicines.org.uk/emc/product/1757/smpc","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2023/209501s005lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Capsule; oral solution; extended-release tablet for non-epilepsy indications","field":"formulations_available","proposed_value":"Capsule; oral solution; extended-release tablet for non-epilepsy indications","rationale":"FDA labeling supports Lyrica capsules and oral solution for seizure indications; Lyrica CR is an extended-release tablet for neuropathic pain indications and its partial-onset seizure adjunctive trial failed to demonstrate efficacy.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2016/021446s030%2C022488s010lbl.pdf","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2023/209501s005lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Adjunctive focal seizures: 150-600 mg/day divided BID/TID","field":"typical_doses_per_day","proposed_value":"Adjunctive focal seizures: 150-600 mg/day divided BID/TID","rationale":"FDA/eMC labeling supports starting at 150 mg/day and titrating to 600 mg/day, divided BID or TID for partial/focal seizures.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2016/021446s030%2C022488s010lbl.pdf","https://www.medicines.org.uk/emc/product/1757/smpc"]},{"current_value":"150 mg/day","field":"minimum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"150 mg/day","rationale":"FDA labeling states pregabalin 150 to 600 mg/day has been shown effective as adjunctive therapy for adult partial-onset seizures.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2016/021446s030%2C022488s010lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"600 mg/day","field":"maximum_approved_daily_dose","proposed_value":"600 mg/day","rationale":"FDA/eMC seizure dosing supports 600 mg/day as the maximum daily dose for adjunctive partial/focal seizures.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2016/021446s030%2C022488s010lbl.pdf","https://www.medicines.org.uk/emc/product/1757/smpc"]},{"current_value":"Mechanism is not fully elucidated; pregabalin binds alpha-2-delta subunits of voltage-gated calcium channels, which may be involved in anti-seizure effects.","field":"mechanism_of_action","proposed_value":"Mechanism is not fully elucidated; pregabalin binds alpha-2-delta subunits of voltage-gated calcium channels, which may be involved in anti-seizure effects.","rationale":"FDA labeling supports both the alpha-2-delta binding statement and the caveat that the mechanism is not fully elucidated.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2016/021446s030%2C022488s010lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Moderate","field":"mechanism_confidence","proposed_value":"Moderate","rationale":"The FDA label supports the target-binding mechanism but explicitly states the clinical mechanism is not fully elucidated, so moderate confidence is reasonable.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2016/021446s030%2C022488s010lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"~6 h","field":"half_life_range","proposed_value":"~6 h","rationale":"FDA/eMC labeling reports about 6 hours, specifically mean elimination half-life 6.3 hours in normal renal function.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2016/021446s030%2C022488s010lbl.pdf","https://www.medicines.org.uk/emc/product/1757/smpc"]},{"current_value":"Not metabolized; renal excretion","field":"major_organ_for_metabolism","proposed_value":"Not metabolized; renal excretion","rationale":"Pregabalin undergoes negligible metabolism and is eliminated primarily by renal excretion as unchanged drug.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2016/021446s030%2C022488s010lbl.pdf","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/n/livertox/Pregabalin/"]},{"current_value":"Not metabolized; not an enzyme inducer/inhibitor","field":"enzyme_inducing_or_inhibiting","proposed_value":"Not metabolized; not an enzyme inducer/inhibitor","rationale":"FDA/eMC labeling supports negligible metabolism and no clinically relevant CYP inhibition/induction signal.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2016/021446s030%2C022488s010lbl.pdf","https://www.medicines.org.uk/emc/product/1757/smpc"]},{"current_value":"Inducer; No major enzyme effect","field":"filter_enzyme_effect","proposed_value":"No major enzyme effect","rationale":"The row incorrectly includes Inducer. FDA labeling says pregabalin does not inhibit major CYP enzymes and does not induce CYP1A2 or CYP3A4 activity.","requires_user_approval":true,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2016/021446s030%2C022488s010lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"CNS: dizziness 29%, CNS: somnolence 22%, neurologic: ataxia 13%, ophthalmologic: blurred vision 6%, metabolic: weight gain 5%, peripheral: edema 6%","field":"adverse_symptoms_percentages","proposed_value":"CNS: dizziness 32%, CNS: somnolence 22%, neurologic: ataxia 15%, ophthalmologic: blurred vision 10%, metabolic: weight gain 12%, peripheral: edema 5%","rationale":"The current values mix unsupported dose/indication strata. FDA Table 5 for controlled adult adjunctive partial-onset seizure trials gives the all-pregabalin rates listed in the proposed value.","requires_user_approval":true,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2016/021446s030%2C022488s010lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"No clinically meaningful QT effect established","field":"qt_interval_effect","proposed_value":"Rare QT prolongation reported in SmPC; no quantified clinically meaningful QTc effect established from FDA labeling reviewed.","rationale":"The eMC SmPC lists QT prolongation as a rare cardiac adverse reaction, so the current 'No known meaningful QT effect' wording is too absolute.","requires_user_approval":true,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.medicines.org.uk/emc/product/1757/smpc","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2016/021446s030%2C022488s010lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"No known meaningful QT effect","field":"filter_qt_effect","proposed_value":"QT prolongation reported/rare","rationale":"The filter should reflect the SmPC-listed rare QT prolongation rather than categorizing pregabalin as having no known QT effect.","requires_user_approval":true,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.medicines.org.uk/emc/product/1757/smpc"]},{"current_value":"Alzain; Lyrica","field":"trade_names","proposed_value":"Alzain; Lyrica; Lyrica CR; Misabri PR","rationale":"Alzain and Lyrica are verified. Lyrica CR is an FDA-labeled pregabalin extended-release product, and Misabri PR is an eMC-listed pregabalin prolonged-release product. Do not add 'PREGABALIN' as a trade name because it is the generic name, not a distinct trade name.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"missing","supporting_sources":["https://www.medicines.org.uk/emc/product/1757/smpc","https://www.ema.europa.eu/en/medicines/human/EPAR/lyrica","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2023/209501s005lbl.pdf","https://www.medicines.org.uk/emc/product/100373/smpc"]},{"current_value":"","field":"alternate_generic_names","proposed_value":"","rationale":"No separate alternate generic name requiring a CSV alias was identified from trusted labeling sources. CI-1008 is better retained as a search/development alias, not an alternate generic name.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2016/021446s030%2C022488s010lbl.pdf","https://www.ema.europa.eu/en/medicines/human/EPAR/lyrica"]},{"current_value":"CI-1008","field":"pubmed_search_aliases","proposed_value":"CI-1008","rationale":"The alias is plausible as a development/search alias, but the row's named evidence sources do not specifically support it.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"missing_source","supporting_sources":[]},{"current_value":"Current adjunctive ASM for focal/partial seizures; also used for neuropathic pain, fibromyalgia, and generalized anxiety disorder in some markets.","field":"status_or_notes","proposed_value":"Current adjunctive ASM for focal/partial seizures; also used for neuropathic pain, fibromyalgia, and generalized anxiety disorder in some markets.","rationale":"FDA labeling supports partial-onset seizures, neuropathic pain, and fibromyalgia; eMC/SmPC supports generalized anxiety disorder in adults in some markets.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2016/021446s030%2C022488s010lbl.pdf","https://www.medicines.org.uk/emc/product/1757/smpc"]}],"generic_name":"pregabalin","missing_rcts":[],"outcome_checks":[{"current_value":"15-40 % (drug minus placebo RR50 differential at maximum effective dose/regimen: Antinew2019 pregabalin 10 mg/kg/day or 14 mg/kg/day if <30 kg 18%; Baulac2010 pregabalin up to 600 mg/day 15%; Beydoun2005 pregabalin 600 mg/day TID 40%; Arroyo2004 pregabalin 600 mg/day TID 37.3%; French2003 pregabalin 600 mg/day BID 37%)","field":"diff_50_responder_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"15-40 % (drug minus placebo RR50 differential at maximum effective dose/regimen: Antinew2019 pregabalin 10 mg/kg/day or 14 mg/kg/day if <30 kg 18%; Baulac2010 pregabalin up to 600 mg/day 15%; Beydoun2005 pregabalin 600 mg/day TID 40%; Arroyo2004 pregabalin 600 mg/day TID 37.3%; French2003 pregabalin 600 mg/day BID 37%)","rationale":"The RR50 differentials match the cited active-minus-placebo responder rates in the cited records/outcome audit: Antinew 40.6-22.6, Baulac 36-21, Beydoun 49-9, Arroyo 43.5-6.2, French 51-14.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/30688135/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/20696552/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/15699378/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/14692903/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/12771254/","https://www.medicines.org.uk/emc/product/1757/smpc"]},{"current_value":"Mann2020|35|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32189338/|175; Antinew2019|19.9|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/30688135/|295; Baulac2010|20|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/20696552/|434; Elger2005|38.7|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/16393158/|341; Beydoun2005|54|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/15699378/|312; Arroyo2004|49.6|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/14692903/|287; French2003|47|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/12771254/|453","field":"plot_diff_median_pct_change_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"Antinew2019|19.9|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/30688135/|295; Baulac2010|20|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/20696552/|434; Elger2005|38.7|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/16393158/|341; Beydoun2005|54|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/15699378/|312; Arroyo2004|49.6|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/14692903/|287; French2003|47|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/12771254/|453","rationale":"Mann2020 reports a 35% placebo-relative reduction in log-transformed video-EEG seizure rate, not a median percent-change differential. The remaining entries are supported as active-minus-placebo median percent-change/seizure-frequency reduction differentials.","requires_user_approval":true,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32189338/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/30688135/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/20696552/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/16393158/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/15699378/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/14692903/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/12771254/"]},{"current_value":"19.9-54 % (drug minus placebo MPC differential at maximum effective dose/regimen: Mann2020 pregabalin 14 mg/kg/day 35%; Antinew2019 pregabalin 10 mg/kg/day or 14 mg/kg/day if <30 kg 19.9%; Baulac2010 pregabalin up to 600 mg/day 20%; Elger2005 pregabalin 600 mg/day BID fixed dose 38.7%; Beydoun2005 pregabalin 600 mg/day TID 54%; Arroyo2004 pregabalin 600 mg/day TID 49.6%; French2003 pregabalin 600 mg/day BID 47%)","field":"diff_median_pct_change_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"19.9-54 % (drug minus placebo MPC differential at maximum effective dose/regimen: Antinew2019 pregabalin 10 mg/kg/day or 14 mg/kg/day if <30 kg 19.9%; Baulac2010 pregabalin up to 600 mg/day 20%; Elger2005 pregabalin 600 mg/day BID fixed dose 38.7%; Beydoun2005 pregabalin 600 mg/day TID 54%; Arroyo2004 pregabalin 600 mg/day TID 49.6%; French2003 pregabalin 600 mg/day BID 47%). Note: Mann2020 reported a 35% placebo-relative reduction in log-transformed video-EEG seizure rate, not an MPC differential.","rationale":"The range remains 19.9-54 after removing Mann2020 from the MPC rollup. Mann2020's 35% is a different modeled endpoint and should not be labeled median percent change.","requires_user_approval":true,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32189338/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/30688135/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/20696552/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/16393158/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/15699378/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/14692903/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/12771254/"]},{"current_value":"NR/not extractable as a drug-minus-placebo seizure-freedom patient-rate differential at the maximum effective dose/regimen from included phase II/III placebo-controlled RCT records","field":"diff_seizure_freedom_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"NR/not extractable as a drug-minus-placebo seizure-freedom patient-rate differential at the maximum effective dose/regimen from included phase II/III placebo-controlled RCT records","rationale":"The cited placebo-controlled RCT abstracts/outcome audit do not provide an extractable drug-minus-placebo seizure-freedom patient-rate differential for maximum effective dose/regimen. French2014 reports monotherapy/historical-control context and should not be used as a placebo differential.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34033265/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32189338/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/30688135/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24962242/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/20696552/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/19222545/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/16393158/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/15699378/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/14692903/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/12771254/"]}],"overall_status":"needs_update","proposed_row_updates":[{"current_value":"2005","field":"year_fda_cleared","proposed_value":"2004","reason":"FDA label and original approval documentation support Initial U.S. Approval in 2004, not 2005.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2016/021446s030%2C022488s010lbl.pdf","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/nda/2004/021446_Lyrica%20Capsules_approv.PDF"]},{"current_value":"CNS: dizziness 29%, CNS: somnolence 22%, neurologic: ataxia 13%, ophthalmologic: blurred vision 6%, metabolic: weight gain 5%, peripheral: edema 6%","field":"adverse_symptoms_percentages","proposed_value":"CNS: dizziness 32%, CNS: somnolence 22%, neurologic: ataxia 15%, ophthalmologic: blurred vision 10%, metabolic: weight gain 12%, peripheral: edema 5%","reason":"Use a single FDA-supported adverse-event stratum: all pregabalin-treated patients in controlled adult adjunctive partial-onset seizure trials.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2016/021446s030%2C022488s010lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Inducer; No major enzyme effect","field":"filter_enzyme_effect","proposed_value":"No major enzyme effect","reason":"Pregabalin is not a CYP enzyme inducer in FDA labeling.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2016/021446s030%2C022488s010lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"No clinically meaningful QT effect established","field":"qt_interval_effect","proposed_value":"Rare QT prolongation reported in SmPC; no quantified clinically meaningful QTc effect established from FDA labeling reviewed.","reason":"eMC SmPC lists QT prolongation as a rare cardiac adverse reaction.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://www.medicines.org.uk/emc/product/1757/smpc"]},{"current_value":"No known meaningful QT effect","field":"filter_qt_effect","proposed_value":"QT prolongation reported/rare","reason":"The existing filter is too absolute in light of SmPC-listed rare QT prolongation.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://www.medicines.org.uk/emc/product/1757/smpc"]},{"current_value":"Alzain; Lyrica","field":"trade_names","proposed_value":"Alzain; Lyrica; Lyrica CR; Misabri PR","reason":"Adds verified pregabalin brand/formulation names and avoids treating aliases as separate drugs. Do not add PREGABALIN as a trade name.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.medicines.org.uk/emc/product/1757/smpc","https://www.ema.europa.eu/en/medicines/human/EPAR/lyrica","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2023/209501s005lbl.pdf","https://www.medicines.org.uk/emc/product/100373/smpc"]},{"current_value":"No FDA boxed warning identified in selected current DailyMed label.","field":"fda_black_box_warning","proposed_value":"No FDA boxed warning identified in selected current FDA/openFDA label.","reason":"DailyMed is not permissible for boxed-warning verification; use FDA/openFDA wording.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%22f280bbd8-2af2-444a-bd96-e409337ca6dd%22&limit=5"]},{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed SPL; status=no_boxed_warning_in_selected_label; setid=f280bbd8-2af2-444a-bd96-e409337ca6dd; published=Apr 15, 2026; title=LYRICA CR (PREGABALIN) TABLET, FILM COATED, EXTENDED RELEASE [VIATRIS SPECIALTY LLC]; url=https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=f280bbd8-2af2-444a-bd96-e409337ca6dd","field":"fda_black_box_warning_source","proposed_value":"FDA/openFDA drug label API; status=no_boxed_warning_in_selected_fda_label; spl_set_id=f280bbd8-2af2-444a-bd96-e409337ca6dd; effective_time=20260312; title=Lyrica CR / PREGABALIN; api_url=https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%22f280bbd8-2af2-444a-bd96-e409337ca6dd%22&limit=5","reason":"Replaces the nonpermissible DailyMed boxed-warning source with FDA/openFDA metadata.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%22f280bbd8-2af2-444a-bd96-e409337ca6dd%22&limit=5"]},{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed labeling","field":"mechanism_source","proposed_value":"FDA/accessdata labeling","reason":"The mechanism is supported by FDA label text; cite FDA/accessdata rather than DailyMed under the row's trusted-source policy.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2016/021446s030%2C022488s010lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"NCBI LiverTox anticonvulsants table; Epilepsy Society ASM list; Epilepsy Foundation Australia ASM list; FDA/DailyMed labeling","field":"evidence_sources","proposed_value":"FDA/accessdata labeling; FDA/openFDA labeling; FDA Drugs@FDA approval documents; PubMed RCT abstracts; ClinicalTrials.gov trial records; NCBI LiverTox pregabalin page and anticonvulsants table; EMA EPAR/eMC SmPC","reason":"Current row sources include non-trusted or nonspecific sources for this audit policy, and DailyMed should not be used for the FDA boxed-warning field.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2016/021446s030%2C022488s010lbl.pdf","https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%22f280bbd8-2af2-444a-bd96-e409337ca6dd%22&limit=5","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/n/livertox/Pregabalin/","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK548365/table/Anticonvulsants.Tc/","https://www.ema.europa.eu/en/medicines/human/EPAR/lyrica","https://www.medicines.org.uk/emc/product/1757/smpc"]},{"current_value":"Driscoll2021|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34033265/; Mann2020|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32189338/; Antinew2019|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/30688135/; French2014b|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24962242/; French2014|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24415567/; Baulac2010|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/20696552/; Lee2009|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/19222545/; Elger2005|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/16393158/; Beydoun2005|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/15699378/; Arroyo2004|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/14692903/; French2003|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/12771254/","field":"pubmed_phase_ii_iii_rct_links","proposed_value":"Driscoll2021|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34033265/; Mann2020|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32189338/; Antinew2019|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/30688135/; French2014b|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24962242/; Baulac2010|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/20696552/; Lee2009|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/19222545/; Elger2005|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/16393158/; Beydoun2005|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/15699378/; Arroyo2004|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/14692903/; French2003|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/12771254/","reason":"French2014 is a historical-controlled monotherapy trial and does not have a concurrent placebo arm, so it should not be retained in a placebo-controlled RCT link field.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24415567/"]},{"current_value":"19.9-54 % (drug minus placebo MPC differential at maximum effective dose/regimen: Mann2020 pregabalin 14 mg/kg/day 35%; Antinew2019 pregabalin 10 mg/kg/day or 14 mg/kg/day if <30 kg 19.9%; Baulac2010 pregabalin up to 600 mg/day 20%; Elger2005 pregabalin 600 mg/day BID fixed dose 38.7%; Beydoun2005 pregabalin 600 mg/day TID 54%; Arroyo2004 pregabalin 600 mg/day TID 49.6%; French2003 pregabalin 600 mg/day BID 47%)","field":"diff_median_pct_change_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"19.9-54 % (drug minus placebo MPC differential at maximum effective dose/regimen: Antinew2019 pregabalin 10 mg/kg/day or 14 mg/kg/day if <30 kg 19.9%; Baulac2010 pregabalin up to 600 mg/day 20%; Elger2005 pregabalin 600 mg/day BID fixed dose 38.7%; Beydoun2005 pregabalin 600 mg/day TID 54%; Arroyo2004 pregabalin 600 mg/day TID 49.6%; French2003 pregabalin 600 mg/day BID 47%). Note: Mann2020 reported a 35% placebo-relative reduction in log-transformed video-EEG seizure rate, not an MPC differential.","reason":"Mann2020's endpoint is not a median percent-change differential.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32189338/"]},{"current_value":"Mann2020|35|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32189338/|175; Antinew2019|19.9|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/30688135/|295; Baulac2010|20|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/20696552/|434; Elger2005|38.7|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/16393158/|341; Beydoun2005|54|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/15699378/|312; Arroyo2004|49.6|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/14692903/|287; French2003|47|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/12771254/|453","field":"plot_diff_median_pct_change_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"Antinew2019|19.9|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/30688135/|295; Baulac2010|20|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/20696552/|434; Elger2005|38.7|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/16393158/|341; Beydoun2005|54|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/15699378/|312; Arroyo2004|49.6|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/14692903/|287; French2003|47|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/12771254/|453","reason":"Remove Mann2020 from the median percent-change plot because its 35% value is a different endpoint type.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32189338/"]}],"rct_link_checks":[{"label":"Driscoll2021","pmid":"34033265","proposed_action":"Keep in RCT links, but do not use for focal maximum-effective-dose outcome rollups because it studied generalized tonic-clonic seizures and was not positive versus placebo.","rationale":"PubMed identifies a randomized placebo-controlled trial of adjunctive pregabalin for generalized tonic-clonic seizures with ClinicalTrials.gov NCT01747915.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34033265/"},{"label":"Mann2020","pmid":"32189338","proposed_action":"Keep in RCT links; do not label its 35% value as median percent change.","rationale":"The record is a double-blind placebo-controlled video-EEG trial in children with focal-onset seizures, but the cited 35% outcome is a placebo-relative log-transformed seizure-rate reduction.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32189338/"},{"label":"Antinew2019","pmid":"30688135","proposed_action":"Keep.","rationale":"Supported as a randomized placebo-controlled adjunctive pregabalin trial for pediatric focal-onset seizures; RR50 40.6% versus 22.6% placebo supports the 18% differential.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/30688135/"},{"label":"French2014b","pmid":"24962242","proposed_action":"Keep, but do not use in positive maximum-effective-dose rollups.","rationale":"Controlled-release pregabalin trial was randomized and placebo-controlled but did not demonstrate efficacy versus placebo.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24962242/"},{"label":"French2014","pmid":"24415567","proposed_action":"Remove from pubmed_phase_ii_iii_rct_links or move to a non-placebo/historical-control notes field.","rationale":"The title and outcome audit identify this as a historical-controlled pregabalin monotherapy trial, not a concurrent placebo-controlled RCT; it cannot support drug-minus-placebo outcome differentials.","status":"not_placebo_rct","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24415567/"},{"label":"Baulac2010","pmid":"20696552","proposed_action":"Keep; disregard the deterministic title-only warning as a false positive.","rationale":"The abstract describes randomization to pregabalin, lamotrigine, or placebo as adjunctive therapy, and reports pregabalin responder rate 36% versus placebo 21% and median reduction versus placebo.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/20696552/"},{"label":"Lee2009","pmid":"19222545","proposed_action":"Keep; do not use for RR50/MPC/SF rollups unless extractable values are obtained from full text.","rationale":"The title and row audit identify a double-blind randomized placebo-controlled multicenter flexible-dose pregabalin add-on trial, but abstract-level outcome values are not extractable for the plotted endpoints.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/19222545/"},{"label":"Elger2005","pmid":"16393158","proposed_action":"Keep.","rationale":"Double-blind placebo-controlled pregabalin add-on study; the 600 mg/day fixed-dose arm supports the 38.7% MPC differential in the row audit.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/16393158/"},{"label":"Beydoun2005","pmid":"15699378","proposed_action":"Keep; disregard the deterministic warning as a false positive.","rationale":"The abstract states this was a multicenter double-blind randomized parallel-group placebo-controlled trial of pregabalin 600 mg/day BID or TID versus placebo in partial epilepsy, with responder and seizure-frequency outcomes matching the row.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/15699378/"},{"label":"Arroyo2004","pmid":"14692903","proposed_action":"Keep.","rationale":"Randomized double-blind placebo-controlled dose-response add-on study in adults with partial seizures; outcome values match the row audit.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/14692903/"},{"label":"French2003","pmid":"12771254","proposed_action":"Keep.","rationale":"PubMed abstract verifies a 76-center double-blind randomized placebo-controlled parallel-group trial in partial seizures; 600 mg/day BID had 54% seizure-frequency reduction versus 7% placebo and 51% RR50 versus 14% placebo.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/12771254/"}],"source_updates":[{"current_value":"NCBI LiverTox anticonvulsants table; Epilepsy Society ASM list; Epilepsy Foundation Australia ASM list; FDA/DailyMed labeling","field":"evidence_sources","proposed_value":"FDA/accessdata labeling; FDA/openFDA labeling; FDA Drugs@FDA approval documents; PubMed RCT abstracts; ClinicalTrials.gov trial records; NCBI LiverTox pregabalin page and anticonvulsants table; EMA EPAR/eMC SmPC","reason":"Use named trusted sources that directly support row facts; remove non-trusted/nonspecific list sources for this audit policy and avoid DailyMed for boxed-warning verification.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2016/021446s030%2C022488s010lbl.pdf","https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%22f280bbd8-2af2-444a-bd96-e409337ca6dd%22&limit=5","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/n/livertox/Pregabalin/","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK548365/table/Anticonvulsants.Tc/","https://www.ema.europa.eu/en/medicines/human/EPAR/lyrica","https://www.medicines.org.uk/emc/product/1757/smpc"]},{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed labeling","field":"mechanism_source","proposed_value":"FDA/accessdata labeling","reason":"Mechanism text is supported by FDA label text; DailyMed is unnecessary and not in the trusted-source list supplied for this audit.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2016/021446s030%2C022488s010lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed SPL; status=no_boxed_warning_in_selected_label; setid=f280bbd8-2af2-444a-bd96-e409337ca6dd; published=Apr 15, 2026; title=LYRICA CR (PREGABALIN) TABLET, FILM COATED, EXTENDED RELEASE [VIATRIS SPECIALTY LLC]; url=https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=f280bbd8-2af2-444a-bd96-e409337ca6dd","field":"fda_black_box_warning_source","proposed_value":"FDA/openFDA drug label API; status=no_boxed_warning_in_selected_fda_label; spl_set_id=f280bbd8-2af2-444a-bd96-e409337ca6dd; effective_time=20260312; title=Lyrica CR / PREGABALIN; api_url=https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%22f280bbd8-2af2-444a-bd96-e409337ca6dd%22&limit=5","reason":"FDA boxed-warning verification must use FDA/openFDA, FDA labels, or Drugs@FDA; DailyMed is not permissible for this field.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%22f280bbd8-2af2-444a-bd96-e409337ca6dd%22&limit=5"]}],"summary":"Pregabalin row needs updates. Major issues: FDA approval year should be 2004, adverse-event percentages should be normalized to the FDA epilepsy trial table, the enzyme filter incorrectly says Inducer, QT wording is too absolute because eMC lists rare QT prolongation, DailyMed must be removed from boxed-warning verification, French2014 is not a placebo-controlled RCT, and Mann2020's 35% endpoint is not a median percent-change differential. Baulac2010 and Beydoun2005 are valid pregabalin placebo-controlled RCTs despite the deterministic warning flags."}
